# Deliberately no catch-all rewrite.
#
# Every route is built as its own file (index.html, photos.html, blog.html,
# blog/<slug>.html), so nothing needs rewriting to boot the app — and sending
# `/* /index.html 200` would answer 200 for every mistyped path, which invites a
# search engine to index an unbounded set of duplicate pages and leaves an agent
# unable to tell a wrong URL from a right one.
#
# Unmatched requests fall through to 404.html, which Cloudflare Pages serves
# with a real 404. React still boots there and renders the NotFound page.
